backend/data/pfs_rates_2025.csv
.claude/

# Generated ops board. Local only — it carries subscriber data.
backend/data/whatholdsup/dashboard.html

# The source library's DOCUMENTS. This repository is public.
#
# The library holds the papers, labels, registry postings and guidelines the
# issues are checked against, so that a sentence can be reopened against the
# bytes it came from. Some of those documents are subscription content — three
# NEJM papers were downloaded through the editor's own access on 2026-09-01 —
# and putting them in a public repository would be republishing them.
#
# The MANIFESTS stay in git: backend/data/whatholdsup/library/index.json and
# library/issues/*.json carry the sha256, the URL, how it was obtained, and
# whether the bytes are the full text, an abstract or a page about it. What we
# hold and what that licenses is the public record; the copyrighted bytes are
# a local archive.
#
# A clone therefore verifies the manifests and re-acquires the documents. Run
#   backend/venv/bin/python3 scripts/whatholdsup/source_store.py <slug> gaps
# to see what is missing.
backend/data/whatholdsup/library/docs/
